  "body": "Step out from the upstairs living room onto the deck and take in the broad sweep of Lake Pupuke. The main bedroom shares the lake outlook, while the home’s north-west aspect draws in the afternoon sun. There are glimpses of the sea, too. Set between the lake and the coast on Takapuna’s Golden Mile, the property is within easy reach of Takapuna Beach, local cafés and restaurants, and Milford Village.\r\n\r\nWith four bedrooms, two bathrooms and a separate study, the existing home offers a practical layout for buyers who want to make this address their own. Renovate at your own pace, with plans prepared by the previous owner available for reference. A future upper level could open up wider sea views, subject to design and the necessary approvals.\r\n\r\nFor buyers considering development, Auckland Council has granted resource consents to build three contemporary standalone homes and subdivide the approximately 607 sq m site into three freehold lots. The approved plans and consent documents are available for buyers to review as part of their own due diligence.\r\n\r\nImages of the proposed homes are artist's impressions, indicative only, and depict improvements that do not currently exist. Architectural drawings for the consented three-home development are available in the property information pack. Any future development remains subject to building consent and other necessary approvals. Purchasers should undertake their own due diligence and seek independent advice.\r\n\r\nThe owners are committed to selling. Contact Nico Zhang at New Zealand Sotheby's International Realty to arrange a viewing and request the property information pack.",
